70: ## 6. Architecture
71: 
72: A diagram is at `docs/presentation/architecture.png`.
73: 
74: - Browser workspace: React and TypeScript, hash routing, a single persistent store, browser-local persistence with exit flush and visible storage failure, validated JSON backups at schema version 3.
75: - Deterministic core in `src/lib/`: curriculum constraints and diffs, teaching plans, evidence calculations (citation validator, fingerprints, Wilson intervals, coverage stages, report and brief), board payload normalisation and keyword filters, backup validation.
76: - Local API: Hono on Node 24. `/api/parse` for xlsx, csv, pdf, pptx and docx. `/api/collect/:provider/:board` for the two permitted job-board hosts, with board-token validation, a one-hour cache, a 15-second gap between fetches of the same board, at most 20 fetches per ten minutes, a 15 MB size cap, a 20-second timeout and plain error messages. `/api/agent` for optional model streaming with a deterministic fallback.
77: - Planned: a shared API and identity (plan W02) as the contract for Teams through Copilot Studio, Slack and LTI surfaces, so a university reaches Lyceum from the tools it already uses.
78: 
79: ## 7. Data, sources and policies
80: 
81: - Source policies are shown in the app for each collection source: owner, method, retention, refresh, policy review date and a note on intended use. Greenhouse and Lever publish these APIs for employers' career pages; Lyceum fetches a named employer's board at low volume on request and does not collect from LinkedIn or anything behind a login. Scheduled or bulk collection would need confirmation of intended use first.
82: - Provenance per source: lecturer-supplied or collected, with provider, board, posting id, retrieval time and policy label. Publication dates are shown as published and never manufactured from the retrieval time.
83: - Everything is stored in the lecturer's browser. Backups may contain course material and uploaded learner records and belong to the lecturer. No data is sent to a provider unless a model key is configured, and then only the payload of the specific request.
84: 
85: ## 8. Known limitations and not built
86: 
87: - No shared accounts, server permissions, server store or multi-device sync; the browser is the only persistence, with JSON backups as the recovery path.
88: - Collection covers two documented board APIs and manual paste. No page collectors for employer sites without an API, no snapshots of arbitrary sites, no cross-site vacancy clustering, no scheduled refresh.
89: - The Lever API does not state the employer name, so the site token is used.
90: - No comparable time windows yet, so no trend over time is reported.
91: - Assessment items are template-based; exact mark allocation, model answers and rubrics are pending.
92: - Slide packs are generated from saved data with no model-written text. Model-drafted slide content with lecturer review, selective regeneration, institutional templates, handouts, and DOCX or PDF export of the brief are pending.
93: - The Trends, Relevance Index, Acceptance test and Closed loop screens remain on synthetic fixtures and should be quarantined from the lecturer's navigation.
94: - The optional model integration uses an older SDK and a previous-generation model id; the intake route forces a tool call that current models reject. This is scheduled work.
95: - Accessibility: labels, focus, keyboard tabs, reflow and contrast are checked by the smokes; a full WCAG 2.2 AA audit with a screen reader is pending.
96: - No lecturer pilot has run; no educational or commercial validation is claimed.
97: 
98: ## 9. Next steps
99: 
100: In order: quarantine the synthetic screens; the provider upgrade; comparable time windows for trends; employer naming for Lever; model-drafted slide content with lecturer review on top of the deterministic packs; DOCX and PDF export of the brief; code splitting; an accessibility pass; an OpenAPI description of collect, report and brief as the contract for the shared API; the shared API and identity when a pilot has a date; then the Teams or Slack surface for the pilot institution's tool.
101: 
