70: **4. Student-simulation benchmark**
71: 
72: Define the target first: **the probability that a learner meets a specified CLO threshold on a specified assessment in a specified term and course version**. A course-wide scenario score cannot be presented as this prediction without changing and evaluating the model.
73: 
74: Use lecturer-approved, CLO-linked assessment results as the attainment reference. Surveys measure confidence, perceived difficulty or experience separately. Never convert a self-rating directly into demonstrated mastery.
75: 
76: **Minimal exploratory dataset:** one course, three CLOs, two successive cohorts of approximately 30 consenting learners each. This supports a feasibility study, not general validation.
77: 
78: Retain:
79: 
80: - Pseudonymous learner ID, cohort, term, course version and assessment date.
81: - Item ID, CLO mapping, rubric, maximum marks, earned marks and predefined attainment threshold.
82: - Survey question wording, scale anchors, CLO, collection date, response and missingness.
83: - Prediction timestamp, model version, inputs available then and frozen predicted probability.
84: 
85: Use the earlier cohort for development and freeze the model before evaluating the later cohort. Do not mix records from one learner across development and evaluation. Match course version, assessment and term explicitly; upload date alone is insufficient.
86: 
87: Compare against a prior-cohort CLO attainment-rate baseline and a simple prior-performance baseline.
88: 
89: | Measure | What the interface shows |
90: |---|---|
91: | Observed attainment | Learners meeting threshold divided by learners assessed, per CLO. |
92: | Probability error | Brier score for model and baselines, with sample size and uncertainty. |
93: | Calibration | Predicted versus observed attainment, with bin counts; suppress unstable summaries. |
94: | Aggregate error | Absolute percentage-point error per CLO. |
95: | Survey comparison | Response distribution, response rate and association with measured attainment. |
96: | Data quality | Unmatched records, missing assessments, missing surveys and version mismatches. |
97: 
98: Display â€œBenchmark unavailableâ€ when matching data is absent. Register success criteria before evaluation. Better prediction would still not demonstrate that a proposed curriculum change causes learning gains.
